 34AL    9BE(40AR,34AL)                2017HA23,2017HA34         ENSDF    202609
 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL c  2017Ha23, 2017Ha34: a 69.2-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was        
 34AL2c  produced by the Sector Focusing Cyclotron and Separated Sector         
 34AL3c  Cyclotron at the Heavy Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL). The   
 34AL4c  secondary beam containing {+34}Al was produced via the projectile      
 34AL5c  fragmentation of {+40}Ca impinging on a 182.6-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target  
 34AL6c  and was selected using |DE-tof-B|r by the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in 
 34AL7c  Lanzhou (RIBLL). The secondary beam ions were transported into a target
 34AL8c  chamber filled with low-temperature nitrogen and implanted into a      
 34AL9c  1500-|mm-thick DSSD sandwiched between two 3000-|mm-thick plastic      
 34ALAc  scintillators for beam diagnostics and veto, respectively. |g rays were
 34ALBc  detected using two Ge clover detectors. The fast timing signals of the 
 34ALCc  |g rays were provided by a lanthanum bromide (LaBr{-3}) detector.      
 34ALDc  Neutrons were detected using two plastic scintillator arrays. Measured 
 34ALEc  implant-|b correlation, E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, and |bn-coin.  
 34ALFc  Deduced levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, parent       
 34ALGc  {+34}Al and {+34}Al isomer T{-1/2}. Comparisons with shell-model       
 34ALHc  calculations using Gogny D1S and SDPF-M interactions. Also see 2019Wa38
 34ALIc  for detection setup.                                                   
 34AL cL E,J$From the Adopted Levels.                                           
 34AL  L 0            4-               51.5 MS   9                              
 34AL cL T$from fit of implant-|b-929|g decay curve (2017Ha23, 2017Ha34).       
 34AL  L 46.56     11 1+               21.6 MS   15                          M  
 34AL cL T$from fit of implant-|b-1193|g decay curve (2017Ha23, 2017Ha34). A    
 34AL2cL total of 6.5|*10{+5} 46.6-keV isomer decay events were observed in     
 34AL3cL 2017Ha23 from fit of the inclusive |b decay curve.                     

